Your Google OAuth setup is working—the error comes from StayonSite's **invite-only** check in [auth.ts](file:///Users/ar/Documents/code/stayonsite/site/worker/auth.ts#L102-L112):

```ts
databaseHooks: {
  user: {
    create: {
      // Invite-only, for every sign-in method: the email must be verified
      // by the provider (or the OTP) and have a pending invite.
      async before(user) {
        const invite = user.emailVerified ? await inviteFor(user.email) : null;
        if (!invite)
          throw new APIError("FORBIDDEN", {
            message: "This email hasn't been invited to StayonSite.",
          });
```

When you sign in with Google for the first time, it tries to create a user record, checks `inviteFor(user.email)` in your local D1 database, and rejects the sign-in because that email doesn't have a pending invite yet.

To fix it, invite that email address in your local D1 database (or seed an invite / admin user for it) before signing in.

